<title>USA: U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</title>
<headline>U.S. cotton weekly export sales highlights - USDA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>USDA cotton export sales highlights in latest reporting week:</p>
<p>Net Upland sales of 97,000 running bales (RB) exceeded the previous week by 13 percent and the 4-week average by 17 percent.  Major increases for Mexico (36,800 RB), China (36,200 RB), Taiwan (13,100 RB), Indonesia (6,200 RB), and South Korea (6,200 RB) were partially offset by reductions of 7,800 RB for Hong Kong.</p>
<p>Exports of 91,200 RB were 38 percent below the previous week and the 4-week average.  Asian destinations accounted for 68 percent of the week's shipments; Western Hemisphere, 18 percent; West European, 12 percent; and East European, 2 percent.</p>
</text>
